    "created_at": "2016-07-12T16:07:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-12T16:07:29Z",
    "body": "Nice catch.\n\nThis appears to have regressed in https://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/8a31542bae88376c33c9d0d8be9fe956409cbf7c.\n\nLooking at the code before that commit, it seems like the correct fix would be to change\n\n> If new is true, then replacement must be enabled.\n\nto\n\n> If new is true or replace is true, then replacement must be enabled.\n\nOn the other hand:\n- [Chrome does not use this argument](https://cs.chromium.org/chromium/src/third_party/WebKit/Source/core/frame/Window.idl?q=window.idl&sq=package:chromium&l=65) (verified by checking C++ custom bindings)\n- [WebKit does not use this argument](https://github.com/WebKit/webkit/blob/5cedd5a28c8871b792e5c3524ba10cd2b8a083f3/Source/WebCore/page/DOMWindow.idl#L68) (verified by checking C++ custom bindings)\n- [Gecko does not seem to use this argument](http://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/source/dom/webidl/Window.webidl#62) (although I wasn't sure where to check to find their corresponding C++)\n\nThere must be history here...\n",
